  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Response to Cyclone-Affected Populations in Vanuatu with Lifesaving Shelter and Non-food Items (ES/NFI)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Vanuatu&#x2019;s National Disaster Management Office (NDMO) estimates that more than 250,000 people (approximately 80 per cent of the entire population of Vanuatu) were affected by Tropical Cyclones Judy and Kevin, which made landfall between 1 -3 March 2023. IOM is working in partnership with the NDMO and partners such as Vanuatu Red Cross and CARE to deliver lifesaving assistance to people impacted by the cyclones. The Displacement and Evacuation Centre Management cluster, co -led by NDMO and IOM is utilising displacement tracking tools to help with coordination of the multi-partner relief efforts to ensure that the right assistance gets to the populations who need it most. Through this project, IOM is focusing on Shelter and Non -Food Items (S/NFIs) assistance, using cash-based or in-kind modality, as well as providing support to evacuation centres and tracking displacement and population mobility.</narrative>
  </description>
